From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 17:30:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile.master.64: drop the 64-bit tool overrides

`Makefile.master.64` overrides `CC`, `CCC`, `CPP`, `AS`, `LD` and their
`NATIVE*` counterparts with the `*64` variants, and swaps `BUILD.SO` for
`BUILD64.SO`. That indirection exists so one build can drive both a 32- and
a 64-bit compiler.

A Nix cross-build has exactly one compiler, already configured for the right
target by the wrapper, so these overrides only serve to point the build at
tools that do not exist. The `-64` mapfile handling below them is still
needed and is left alone.
---
 usr/src/Makefile.master.64 | 17 -----------------
 1 file changed, 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/Makefile.master.64 b/usr/src/Makefile.master.64
index 82aedf6a7a..a3536d0e6e 100644
--- a/usr/src/Makefile.master.64
+++ b/usr/src/Makefile.master.64
@@ -58,23 +58,6 @@ LDLIBS.lib =	$(LDLIBS64)
 #
 GCCLIBDIR=	$(GCCLIBDIR64)
 
-#
-# Override Makefile.master's settings
-#
-CC=		$(CC64)
-CCC=		$(CCC64)
-CPP=		$(CPP64)
-AS=		$(AS64)
-LD=		$(LD64)
-NATIVECC=	$(NATIVECC64)
-NATIVECCC=	$(NATIVECCC64)
-NATIVECPP=	$(NATIVECPP64)
-NATIVEAS=	$(NATIVEAS64)
-NATIVELD=	$(NATIVELD64)
-
-BUILD.SO=	$(BUILD64.SO)
-BUILDCCC.SO=	$(BUILDCCC64.SO)
-
 #
 # ld(1) requires the -64 option to create a 64-bit filter solely from a mapfile
 #
